# Caddy terminates HTTPS (automatic certificates) and proxies to the app on 127.0.0.1:8765.
# NECRO_SITE is the public hostname, for example necro.example.com or 203-0-113-10.sslip.io.
# It comes from /etc/necromancer/caddy.env (see deploy/RUNBOOK.md).
#
# What the app needs from the proxy:
#  * Host is forwarded unchanged (Caddy's default). voice/server.py refuses a WebSocket upgrade when
#    the Origin host differs from the Host it receives, so do NOT add `header_up Host ...`.
#  * WebSocket upgrades pass through (Caddy handles Upgrade/Connection itself; no idle timeout).
#  * The app sees every visitor as 127.0.0.1. With NECRO_TRUST_PROXY=1 (set in necromancer.env) it
#    rate-limits wrong codes per visitor using the X-Forwarded-For entry Caddy writes (Caddy 2.5+ drops
#    any value a client sends). Do NOT add trusted_proxies here: Caddy faces the internet directly.
# To test without Let's Encrypt production rate limits, add a global block at the top:
#   { acme_ca https://acme-staging-v02.api.letsencrypt.org/directory }

{$NECRO_SITE} {
	reverse_proxy {$NECRO_UPSTREAM:127.0.0.1:8765}
	header {
		Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=86400"
		X-Content-Type-Options "nosniff"
		-Server
	}
}
